<title>UK: LME copper barely weaker in late trading.</title>
<headline>LME copper barely weaker in late trading.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>LME copper was slightly easier in late inter-office trading on Tuesday evening, but still locked in its range.</p>
<p>At 1800 GMT, three months copper was indicated at $2,350/55 per tonne, down a touch from an afternoon kerb close of $2,360.</p>
<p>Prices are expected to continue to remain within a $2,320-$2,380 range in the near-term, traders said.</p>
<p>Other metals were little changed.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542-8065</p>
</text>
